B.b6v=A.a(s(["Apply herbicides early morning or late evening (calm winds & high humidity) for peak absorption.","Rotate herbicide mode-of-action groups (HRAC classes) annually to prevent chemical resistance.",'Scout fields systematically in a "W" or "Z" pattern weekly during peak emergence periods.',"Use GPS field mapping to spot and treat localized weed hotspots before they spread.","Calibrate sprayer nozzles regularly; worn tips cause uneven coverage and herbicide waste.","Integrate cereal rye or clover cover crops between seasons to naturally suppress weed seed germination.","Maintain clean field borders and bunds \u2014 weed seed banks travel easily via wind and water.","Deep summer ploughing exposes perennial weed rhizomes and tubers to direct solar heat.","Apply pre-emergent herbicides right after rainfall or irrigation when soil moisture is optimal.","Ensure sprayer water pH is between 5.5 and 6.5; alkaline water can deactivate glyphosate and glufosinate.","Intercropping with leguminous crops provides living mulch and smothers early grass weeds.","Target post-emergent spraying when weeds are in the tender 2-to-4 leaf stage for maximum efficacy.","Thoroughly wash tractors and harvesters before entering clean fields to stop weed seed transfer.","Incorporate mechanical weeding with a wheel hoe or cultivator between rows before canopy closure.","Adjust sprayer boom height to 50 cm above crop canopy to prevent drift and ensure uniform overlap.","Use certified weed-free crop seed lots to prevent introducing noxious foreign weed species.","High-density planting narrows inter-row gaps, shading the ground faster and suppressing light-dependent weeds.","Avoid spraying herbicides when wind speed exceeds 10 km/h to prevent spray drift damage.","Apply organic straw or plastic mulching in vegetable beds to block weed emergence completely.","Alternate irrigation methods (drip vs flood) to limit moisture availability in non-crop row zones.","Keep records of persistent weed species per plot to plan targeted pre-plant weed control.","Destroy weed plants before flowering and seed dispersal to deplete the long-term soil seed bank.","Use appropriate non-ionic surfactants or adjuvants when recommended to enhance leaf uptake.","Monitor ditches, drainage channels, and farm roads as common reservoirs for weed infestation.","Allow pre-emergent herbicide spray barrier to remain undisturbed; avoid shallow hoeing right after spraying.","Check weather forecasts before spraying: ensure a 4 to 6-hour rain-free window for foliar uptake.","Test soil nutrient balance regularly; excessive nitrogen fertilization often accelerates aggressive weed growth.","Stale seedbed technique: irrigate field early, allow weeds to sprout, eliminate them, then sow crop.","Clean backpack sprayer tanks with clean water and detergent immediately after completing spraying.","Combine bio-herbicides and manual weeding in organic plots for sustainable weed management.","Early weed competition during the first 30\u201345 days after sowing causes the greatest yield loss."]),t.s)
